/-!
# Flat constructible lifting covers for Noetherian coefficients

Source: `literature/stacks-project/etale-cohomology.tex`, Tag 03TT (lemma-when-ctf),
Tag 095N (lemma-category-constructible-modules), and Tag 03S8 (lemma-jshriek-constructible)
(blueprint: lem-per-noetherian-constructible-flat-lifting).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Etale

/-- Over a Noetherian scheme and a Noetherian coefficient ring, a constructible sheaf admits
an epimorphic cover by a flat constructible finite sum of affine étale lower-shriek constant
rank-one sheaves, and every map from the constructible sheaf lifts through that cover along
an epimorphism.

Source: `literature/stacks-project/etale-cohomology.tex`, Tag 03TT (lemma-when-ctf),
Tag 095N (lemma-category-constructible-modules), and Tag 03S8 (lemma-jshriek-constructible).
(blueprint: lem-per-noetherian-constructible-flat-lifting).

Proof plan:
1. The finite affine Noetherian cover makes X quasi-compact and locally Noetherian.
By lem-weil-pbc-locally-noetherian-quasi-separated it is quasi-separated. By
lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-scheme-closed-subsets-minimal and
lem-sfb-noetherian-space-compact-subsets all subsets are quasi-compact. Every locally closed
stratum is therefore constructible (def-weil-constructible-subset). Apply
lem-per-noetherian-affine-free-presentation to G to obtain an epic finite sum of affine
rank-one lower-shriek sheaves; only its generator part is needed.
2. By lem-weil-pbc-free-etale-module-shriek-comparison each summand is free representable.
The Hom bijection of lem-weil-pbc-sheaf-free-separator and evaluation at 1 identify maps from
it to F with F(U). Thus the component generator maps correspond to sections s_i of G(U_i).
Naturality identifies composition with g and restriction with their sectionwise operations.
3. The exact forgetful functor of lem-weil-pbc-module-sheaves-colimits-forgetful carries p
to an epimorphism of abelian sheaves. By lem-weil-pbc-abelian-sheaf-epi-locally-surjective,
each g(s_i) lifts on a covering sieve. By
lem-weil-pbc-etale-covering-sieve-finite-affine-refinement refine this to finitely many affine
etale V_ik covering U_i, with actual sections t_ik of B lifting g(s_i) on V_ik.
4. Set E to the finite coproduct of the rank-one lower-shriek sheaves for the V_ik.
The restricted s_i and the t_ik define e and h by the Hom bijection in step 2 and the
coproduct property of lem-weil-pbc-module-sheaves-colimits-forgetful. The lifted-section
equalities give h followed by p equal to e followed by g. To prove e epic, test two maps
out of G equal after e: equality on each V_ik glues to equality on U_i by the sheaf axiom,
then the original epic generator family gives equality on G.
5. Each V_ik is affine, hence quasi-compact and quasi-separated.
By lem-per-noetherian-etale-sum-constructible with M=R its rank-one extension is
constructible. R is generated by 1, with no finiteness assumption on its underlying set.
A finite sum is constructible by common refinement of the finite stratifications and
etale trivializing covers; the constant module values are finite sums of finite modules.
6. Each affine-source map is separated by lem-weil-pbc-affine-source-morphism-separated
and quasi-compact by lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-morphism-permanence. It is locally of finite type
because it is etale, hence of finite type (def-weil-finite-type-morphism).
The rank-one constant sheaf is flat since its tensor functor is naturally the identity.
Apply lem-pur-etale-sum-flat-kflat to each summand. Tensor distributes over finite sums,
and finite sums of exact sequences are exact, giving flatness of E.
7. Reindex the finite set of pairs (i,k) by Fin n. When G=0 take n=0 and E=0.
On the empty scheme every module sheaf is zero by the empty-cover sheaf axiom, as also
for the zero coefficient ring. Thus all zero and empty cases are included. -/
theorem exists_noetherian_constructible_flat_lifting
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian X]
    (R : Type (u + 1)) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (B C G : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} R))
    (p : B ⟶ C) [Epi p] (g : G ⟶ C)
    [Scheme.IsConstructibleSheaf G] :
    ∃ (n : ℕ) (U : Fin n → X.Etale), (∀ i, IsAffine (U i).left) ∧
      let E : Sheaf X.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} R) := ∐ fun i : Fin n ↦
        (Etale.etaleLowerShriek (ModuleCat.{u + 1} R) (U i).hom inferInstance).obj
          ((constantSheaf (U i).left.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} R)).obj
            (ModuleCat.of R R))
      ∃ (e : E ⟶ G) (h : E ⟶ B),
        exactFunctor _ _ (tensorLeft E) ∧ Scheme.IsConstructibleSheaf E ∧ Epi e ∧
          h ≫ p = e ≫ g := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Etale
